So I have committed a patch that returns None whenever an atomic 
NA_integer_ is returned to Python. At least this is better than 
returning True.

Atomic integer and real/float are less problematic, so I am inclined to 
leave them as they are for now.

The variable NA_{LOGICAL, INTEGER, REAL} are hopelessly broken until how 
this can be addressed nicely becomes clear.

This plus a handful of patches already committed should make it as a 
version 2.0.2 scheduled for the weekend.


L.




